Gonna disagree ... if you're facing off with a creature with a special
attack, this shuts down their special attack. Liches can't use touch of
death or destroy armor,  amulet-thieves can't steal amulet,  nymphs can
smile at you but can't take anything, werewolves won't give you
lycanthropy,  vampires won't level-drain you, etc.

I *think* the following is also true -- when facing off with
demogorgan, it disables his disease and stun attacks, making him much
less trouble. But I'm not certain of that. Suggest wizmode testing
before trying that in a real game.

I agree that wands o' cancel aren't terribly useful, but the 1 time out
of a 100 they do, you really, really need them.

On a side note, I should state that, in hundreds of games, I have yet
to have a single Bag of Holding to an explosion caused by a wand o'
cancel.   Not that it's impossible,  but this, like so many other YAS
moves,  is best countered by forethought and careful playing.  I can't
tell you how much my game improved when I learned to simply shut it
down and walk away for awhile.   Muchas Gracias to Krysia's Krusader
for teaching me that. 

